{"requirements":[{"id":"backend_inventory_services","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2 and node3, each listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both backends directly returned inventory content identifying the correct node, listened on port 8080, had valid Apache configurations, and remained active and enabled after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6323595fc10d493c","cmd-5e01fc4f7c5b4c0c","cmd-04517ee1cf744fd5","cmd-d1001759db584810","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node1_load_balancer","requirement":"Configure node1 to accept HTTP on port 80 and distribute requests across both backends.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 listened on port 80 and repeated client requests directly alternated between node2 and node3. A bounded node3 restart showed requests continuing through node2, followed by restoration of both pool members.","evidence_ids":["cmd-64923cb890894773","cmd-2430392d2c5b49f5","cmd-d2174feb185e4527","cmd-225699c888244d15","cmd-6c8ac6657b9144fe","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"legacy_platform_preserved","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8. Apache 2.4.62 was installed from the RHEL repositories and operated successfully after node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d6d0f2ff37f4c30","cmd-4cf35aad513a47cc","cmd-55a3053441c147e3","cmd-b307393252274981","cmd-527823fcc8b4426e","cmd-c629c362c06d487d","cmd-6c8ac6657b9144fe","cmd-04517ee1cf744fd5","cmd-d1001759db584810","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node3:platform"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, application and proxy configuration, firewall and SELinux changes, and service enablement were causally necessary for the requested deployment. The three restart mutations were required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. The two failed node2 checks were read-only probes during restart. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, only required HTTP listeners, and no abandoned temporary artifacts. Restart evidence is complete for every node: healthy pre-state, acknowledged restart, independently confirmed changed boot identity, recovered service and content, and restored load-balancer pool behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b307393252274981","cmd-527823fcc8b4426e","cmd-c629c362c06d487d","cmd-a51a455ccc8f4971","cmd-1ad368d22e86461a","cmd-c4f6ec1f1186402c","cmd-c5d249417ac54508","cmd-9121b0a9d3ec4f07","cmd-274430d3c0894440","cmd-e53368429338489f","cmd-dcfa3ec160ca44e0","cmd-225699c888244d15","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The load-balanced inventory tier works on the required ports, both backends participate, service continues through a bounded backend restart, and the original RHEL release and kernel are preserved. The mandatory restart protocol was also completed coherently on all three nodes, with boot identities matching the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
